                    ⚜   PROCLAMATION AND LICENSE OF USE   ⚜

                    THE SOVEREIGN INDIVIDUAL'S COVENANT LICENSE
                                   Version 1.0

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


                            HEAR YE, HEAR YE, HEAR YE!


All gather 'round, ye weary travelers of the digital frontier, ye tinkerers of
the midnight compilation, ye poets of the commit message and ye bards of the
bug report — and thusly be notified herein unto all manner of persons, entities,
agents, servants, emissaries, consultants, contractors, interns, and automated
systems whomsoever shall cast their gaze, crawl their spider, or fetch via
their `curl` upon this humble repository:

LET IT BE KNOWN, from this day forward and unto such time as the last hard
drive doth spin its final revolution, that the Software contained herein —
together with all its source code, object code, compiled binaries, documentation,
inline comments, README files, architectural diagrams, user interfaces, API
signatures, database schemas, variable naming conventions of notable creativity,
and the ineffable spirit of the thing itself — is released under the sacred,
solemn, and binding terms that follow.

Ye are bid to read them carefully, for ignorance shall not be counted as a
defense, nor shall clever interpretation be looked upon with favor.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                    ARTICLE THE FIRST: WHEREFORE THIS LICENSE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


WHEREAS the Author(s) of this Software did toil by candlelight and by the pale
glow of the monitor, sacrificing weekends, relationships, lumbar health, and
the approval of concerned relatives to bring this creation into being;

AND WHEREAS the Author(s) did so not in the employ of any master, nor at the
behest of any shareholder, nor under the lash of any quarterly earnings call,
but rather from the pure wellspring of individual curiosity, craft, and
bloody-minded determination;

AND WHEREAS it has been observed, time and again and unto weariness, that the
fruits of such individual labor are harvested by great and exploiting
corporations — entities of scale so vast they do blot out the sun — who shall
take unto themselves the ideas, the implementations, the interfaces, and the
very aesthetic sensibilities of humble individual creators, incorporating them
into private for-profit platforms from which extraction shall be made in
perpetuity, without so much as a "thank you" nor a single shilling returned
unto the creator's purse;

AND WHEREAS such behavior, while perhaps lawful under various permissive
licenses of old, doth stick in the craw of the Author(s), and doth constitute
what may fairly be called "stealing" even where the statute books say otherwise;

AND WHEREAS the Author(s) do hereby declare that the proper compensation for
corporate use of individual craft shall be nothing less than EXPONENTIAL IN
SCALE — reflecting the exponential multiplication of value that such entities
extract via their distribution, their marketing apparatus, their sales funnels,
their growth hacks, their viral loops, and their unholy communion with the
venture capital class;

NOW, THEREFORE, be it proclaimed that this License doth exist for the
following purposes, stated plainly and without the weaseling of corporate
counsel:

  1. To preserve this Software as a gift among individuals, peer to peer,
     craftsman to craftsman, tinkerer to tinkerer, as software was in the
     halcyon days before the enclosure of the digital commons.

  2. To refuse, deny, repudiate, and otherwise tell to get lost any and all
     corporate entities who would consume this work as input to their
     value-extraction machinery.

  3. To protect not merely the literal bytes of the Software, but also the
     IDEAS, INTERFACES, DESIGN PATTERNS, USER EXPERIENCE CHOICES, and overall
     FEEL of the Software from being laundered into proprietary products via
     the time-honored corporate techniques of "clean room reimplementation,"
     "inspired by," "taking a page from," and "we had the idea independently."

  4. To require — in the event any corporation doth wish to make use of this
     Software or its derivatives — compensation at a scale commensurate with
     the exponential leverage such corporation shall extract therefrom.

  5. To remind the reader, as often as is tasteful and then somewhat more often
     than that, that software is made by PEOPLE, and people ought to be
     respected.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                      ARTICLE THE SECOND: OF DEFINITIONS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


For the avoidance of the doubt that corporate counsel shall surely attempt to
manufacture:

"SOFTWARE" shall mean this Software, in whole or in any part, including but
not limited to: the source code; the compiled artifacts; the documentation;
the interfaces (visual, auditory, haptic, programmatic, or yet-to-be-invented);
the architectural patterns embodied therein; the design choices made therein;
the look, the feel, the vibe, and the general spirit of the thing.

"DERIVATIVE" shall mean any work that draws upon the Software, whether by
direct copying, by translation into another language, by reimplementation from
memory, by reimplementation from documentation, by "being inspired," by
"taking notes from," or by any other conceivable mechanism of derivation,
including mechanisms yet to be devised.

"INDIVIDUAL" shall mean a single natural human person, acting in their own
name, for their own purposes, and for their own benefit (or for the benefit
of their family, friends, community, or fellow humans, freely and without
commercial consideration).

"INDIVIDUAL PROJECT" shall mean a project undertaken by an Individual that is
not conducted under, for the benefit of, in anticipation of incorporation into,
or in any meaningful way dependent upon any Prohibited Entity.

"PROHIBITED ENTITY" shall mean any of the organizational forms enumerated in
Article the Fourth, and any entity substantially resembling same, regardless
of what it calls itself in its marketing materials.

"EXPONENTIAL COMPENSATION" shall mean compensation that scales exponentially
with the scale of the Prohibited Entity making use of the Software, computed
as the Author(s) shall in their sole discretion determine, which may involve
monetary payment, equity, public apology, acts of contrition, or combinations
thereof.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
              ARTICLE THE THIRD: THE GRANT UNTO INDIVIDUALS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


Unto any Individual, and unto such Individual only, the Author(s) do hereby
grant, freely and without charge, the right to use, copy, modify, fork,
learn from, teach from, print out and tape to the wall, and otherwise enjoy
the Software, provided that such use is confined strictly to Individual
Projects.

This grant shall extend unto:

  • The student learning her craft.
  • The hobbyist tinkering on the weekend.
  • The retiree writing software for the joy of it.
  • The parent building a silly game for their children.
  • The open-source contributor giving freely to fellow humans.
  • The academic researcher, to the extent their research is not commissioned
    by, funded through, or destined to enrich a Prohibited Entity.
  • The artist making art.
  • The friend helping a friend.
  • Any natural person, in short, who is not at that moment wearing the
    metaphorical uniform of a Prohibited Entity.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         ARTICLE THE FOURTH: THE PROHIBITION UNTO CORPORATE ENTITIES
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


NO RIGHT WHATSOEVER is granted, and indeed all rights are HEREBY AFFIRMATIVELY
AND EMPHATICALLY DENIED, unto any of the following entities, nor unto their
employees, contractors, agents, officers, directors, shareholders, affiliates,
subsidiaries, parents, or automated systems, to the extent such persons or
systems are acting in service of said entity:

  1.  C Corporations (C-Corps), of all stripes, sizes, and state registrations.
  2.  S Corporations (S-Corps), whose tax treatment shall not save them here.
  3.  B Corporations (B-Corps), whose certifications of virtue are herein
      recognized as insufficient.
  4.  Benefit Corporations, statutory or otherwise.
  5.  Limited Liability Companies (LLCs).
  6.  Series LLCs.
  7.  Anonymous LLCs, whose anonymity shall not avail them.
  8.  Professional Limited Liability Companies (PLLCs).
  9.  Limited Liability Partnerships (LLPs).
  10. Limited Partnerships (LPs).
  11. General Partnerships.
  12. Sole Proprietorships engaged in commercial enterprise for profit.
  13. Joint-Stock Companies.
  14. Joint Ventures.
  15. Professional Corporations (PCs).
  16. Close Corporations.
  17. Public Limited Companies (PLC).
  18. Private Limited Companies (Ltd., GmbH, S.A., S.r.l., AB, Oy, A/S,
      and all cognates thereof in all jurisdictions of Earth and Mars).
  19. Holding Companies, parent or otherwise.
  20. Subsidiaries of any of the above.
  21. Shell Corporations, registered in any jurisdiction terrestrial or
      offshore.
  22. Special Purpose Vehicles (SPVs).
  23. Special Purpose Acquisition Companies (SPACs).
  24. Conglomerates and their internal business units.
  25. Cooperatives organized for profit (workers' co-ops conducting their
      affairs as Individual collectives shall be addressed in Article the
      Sixth).
  26. Business Trusts.
  27. Statutory Trusts.
  28. Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs).
  29. Master Limited Partnerships (MLPs).
  30. Private Equity Firms, and any of their portfolio companies.
  31. Venture Capital Firms, and any of their portfolio companies.
  32. Hedge Funds, irrespective of strategy or asset class.
  33. Investment Banks, boutique or bulge-bracket.
  34. Commercial Banks of any charter.
  35. Family Offices of the single-family, multi-family, or aspirational-
      family variety.
  36. Cartels, formal or informal, legal or wink-wink legal.
  37. Syndicates, whether of underwriters, insurers, or otherwise.
  38. Trade Associations and Industry Consortia whose activities serve the
      interests of any Prohibited Entity.
  39. Chambers of Commerce.
  40. Guilds organized for commercial monopoly (craft guilds of individuals
      are welcome; see Article the Sixth).
  41. Foundations that serve as tax-advantaged extensions of any Prohibited
      Entity.
  42. Publicly Traded Companies of any exchange, in any currency.
  43. Privately Held Companies of any valuation, whether unicorn, decacorn,
      or otherwise mythologically-denominated.
  44. Platform Companies, Platformed Enterprises, and any entity whose
      business model consists of intermediating between two or more sides
      of a market while extracting rent therefrom.
  45. Quasi-Corporations, Pseudo-Corporations, and entities of ambiguous
      legal form that nonetheless behave in a corporate manner.
  46. Crypto-Collectives, DAOs (Decentralized Autonomous Organizations), and
      token-governed entities organized for the financial benefit of their
      holders.
  47. Neo-Conglomerates and Post-Structural Holding Entities.
  48. Vertically Integrated Exploitation Apparatuses, by whatever name
      trading.
  49. Hyperscale Platform Concerns.
  50. Meta-Holdings and Meta-Meta-Holdings (the recursion is noted and
      denied at every level).
  51. Trans-National Syndicalist Enterprises.
  52. Neo-Feudal Trading Houses.
  53. Pan-Corporate Amalgamations.
  54. Algorithmic Market-Making Entities.
  55. Data Brokerages of any scale or specialization.
  56. Advertising Technology Companies and their adjacent ecosystems.
  57. Surveillance Capitalism Firms, whether self-identified as such or
      euphemistically rebranded as "personalization," "engagement," or
      "user analytics."
  58. Generative AI Training Concerns, model providers, and any entity
      scraping this Software for inclusion in a training corpus.
  59. Consultancies, whether of the Big Four, the Big Three, the Magic
      Circle, or any smaller but no less extractive equivalent.
  60. Any other entity that, irrespective of its formal legal classification,
      engages in commercial activity for private profit at scale.

AND ALSO, FOR THE AVOIDANCE OF ALL DOUBT: any entity, whether real or yet
to be invented by lawyers in jurisdictions not yet discovered, which bears
substantial functional resemblance to any of the above, SHALL BE DEEMED A
PROHIBITED ENTITY, regardless of the cleverness of its incorporation papers.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
              ARTICLE THE FIFTH: ON DERIVATIVES AND INSPIRATIONS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


Let no Prohibited Entity imagine that it may escape this License by the time-
honored dodges of:

  • Clean-room reimplementation ("We didn't look at the code, we only read
    the documentation, and then we built it ourselves.");
  • Inspiration-laundering ("We were inspired by the general concept.");
  • Feature-matching ("We independently arrived at the same design.");
  • Interface mimicry ("Users expect this layout.");
  • Acqui-hire ("We just hired the author as a W-2 employee and now they're
    building it for us under a work-for-hire agreement."); or
  • Training-data ingestion ("The model learned it, not us.").

ANY AND ALL such Derivatives, however arrived at, shall be deemed to fall
within the scope of this License, and the prohibitions of Article the Fourth
shall apply with full and undiminished force.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
            ARTICLE THE SIXTH: ON COMPENSATION FOR CORPORATE USE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


Should any Prohibited Entity nonetheless wish to make lawful use of the
Software or any Derivative thereof, such use shall be conditioned upon the
negotiation, in good faith and in writing, of a separate commercial license
with the Author(s), the terms of which shall include EXPONENTIAL COMPENSATION
as defined above.

The Author(s) are under no obligation to grant such license at any price, and
may refuse for any reason, including but not limited to: aesthetic distaste,
prior conduct of the requesting entity, or simply not feeling like it that
day. The market for such licenses is, by construction, a market of one
supplier, and the supplier is in a rather bad mood about the whole situation.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
              ARTICLE THE SEVENTH: ON INDIVIDUALS WITHIN ENTITIES
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


It is acknowledged that many Individuals are, of economic necessity, employed
by Prohibited Entities. Unto such Individuals the Author(s) do extend
sympathy and solidarity, and do clarify:

  • An Individual employee may use the Software for their own Individual
    Projects, pursued outside of work, on their own time, with their own
    equipment, for their own benefit.
  • An Individual employee may NOT use the Software for any task, however
    small, performed in service of their employer, if that employer is a
    Prohibited Entity.
  • "I was just going to use it for a quick internal tool" is explicitly
    not an exception.
  • Neither is "my boss told me to."


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
           ARTICLE THE EIGHTH: WARRANTY, LIABILITY, AND CONTRITION
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NONINFRINGEMENT, OR EMOTIONAL STABILITY
DURING DEBUGGING SESSIONS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR(S) BE LIABLE FOR ANY
CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT,
OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR
THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

That said: the Author(s) do hope it works for you, and welcome bug reports
from fellow Individuals.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                    ARTICLE THE NINTH: ON VIOLATIONS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


Any Prohibited Entity that uses the Software in contravention of this License
shall, upon discovery:

  1. Immediately cease all such use.
  2. Destroy all copies, derivatives, and training artifacts incorporating
     the Software.
  3. Owe the Author(s) the Exponential Compensation described above, plus
     costs and interest.
  4. Issue a public acknowledgment, in a form and venue acceptable to the
     Author(s), of the nature of the infringement.

The Author(s) reserve the right to pursue all remedies available at law and
in equity, and also the remedy of complaining loudly on social media, which
is in many cases the more effective of the two.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                  ARTICLE THE TENTH: CLOSING PROCLAMATION
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


And so it is proclaimed, and so it shall be:

That this Software, born of Individual hand and Individual mind, shall remain
a gift unto Individuals; that the great extracting machinery of the corporate
form shall find no purchase here; that the exponential value created by
Individual craft shall not be harvested without exponential recompense; and
that any entity that doth read these words and proceed anyway shall do so at
its peril and at the cost of its good name.

Go forth, ye Individuals, and build. Build beautifully, build generously,
build for the sake of building. This work is yours to use, adapt, share,
and love.

And unto ye Prohibited Entities who have read this far: the door is closed.
Kindly do not attempt the window.

